1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,400
Stereoplot
Interactive structural data plotting inside QGIS

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,400
Making the most of your structural data
A: bedding and folding · B: folds and lineations · C: large datasets and statistics

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,000
A · Analysis of bedding behaviour
Unveiling the folding pattern

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:17,050
We start with 61 bedding measurements
Zoomed in on the map: strike and dip symbols with dip values

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:22,050
Select them and open the settings dock
Orientation fields are detected automatically; best-fit girdle on

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,450
Poles to bedding spread along a great circle
The best-fit girdle reveals a fold

7
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:28,250
Girdle pole β = 33/347: the fold axis
Woodcock K and fabric strength C are reported on the plot

8
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,250
Which poles might record the hinge zone?
Draw a freehand selection directly on the stereonet

9
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,650
Selected poles are highlighted
Ctrl adds to the selection

10
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:38,850
…and located on the map at the same time
Zoom in to see which outcrops they come from

11
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,400
B · Comparison with fold and lineation measurements
Do the measured structures agree with the bedding?

12
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:44,850
Fold measurements: axes with their axial planes
Lineations with bearing planes, no girdle

13
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:46,850
Classified by concavity
M, S and Z folds get their own colours

14
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:52,450
Some measured fold axes plot close to β
Comparable to the fold axis unveiled by the best-fit girdle on bedding

15
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:57,450
Lineations, classified by type
Intersection (Li) and stretching (Ls) lineations

16
00:00:57,650 --> 00:01:02,450
Intersection lineations follow the fold axis
Li only: the northern cluster sits on β

17
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,000
C · Large-dataset interpretation and statistics
271 cleavage measurements

18
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,650
Foliation–cleavage: 271 measurements
Zoomed to all features in the layer

19
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:10,650
Kamb contours of poles
No great circles, no girdle: just the fabric

20
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:13,450
Mean vector, for reference
Overlays per category, with orientation labels

21
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:17,850
Kamb maximum: steep N–S cleavage (178/79)
It contains the fold axis: an axial-planar fabric

22
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:24,300
Everything in one QGIS panel
Stereonets, contours, girdles, statistics, classification and selection

23
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:28,800
